#!args scenario=Scenario_OneRound seed=42
#
# Regression: every faction's deck must be shuffled before the opening hands are dealt.
#
# InstantiateFactionStates builds each deck straight out of QGData_Decks.json in declaration order
# and hands out card ids sequentially in that same order, and nothing used to disturb it — so the
# opening seven was literally ids 0-6 for Germany and 33-39 for the UK, in every game ever played.
# GameModeMultiplayerDefault.ShuffleDecks now shuffles each deck through GameRandom and replicates
# the result as a ReorderDeckChangeEvent (clients build their decks unshuffled in Init(), and
# ComputeHash covers deck count but not order, so the order has to travel explicitly).
#
# The assertions are pinned to the seed in the #!args line above, but what they are really checking
# is that the ids are NOT the declaration-order run: with the bug, decktop GERMANY is 7 and cards
# 0-6 are all in hand.
# Run:  tests/run-cli.sh tests/qgc/decks_shuffled_at_start.qgc

# The six mandatory opening discards, auto-answered — see opening_turn.qgc.
auto 6

prompt                                  # turn 1, Germany, PLAY_CARD

assert handsize GERMANY == 7
assert decksize GERMANY == 26

# Germany: unshuffled this is card 0 in hand and card 7 on top of the deck.
assert card 0 in deck
assert card 14 in hand
assert decktop GERMANY == 17

# A second faction, because ShuffleDecks has to cover every playable faction and not just the first.
# Unshuffled this is card 33 in hand and card 40 on top of the deck.
assert card 33 in deck
assert card 43 in hand
assert decktop UNITED_KINGDOM == 45

quit
